Z||000002||terryk||05-21-2001||10:08 PM||||Yeah, he should know.<P>Is it the 8253 ECM or the 1470? 90's I believe are 8253's.<P>What color are the wires?<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 05-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eric_PA||05-22-2001||09:43 AM||||I'll check today when I get home from work to see what ECM it is. Off hand three of the wires are dark green with no tracers, they run from the engine compartment, I believe they are AC. The others I remember off hand are Purple, and there is a brown/white wire that comes from the ECM and then also tied together to another brown/white wire going to the engine compartment. I also can't find the check engine light output. I'm thinking that is the brown/white, but why two wires, one going to the engine compartment and the other to the ECM. I will have to check tonight with the harness next to me. There are a few other wires that I can't recall.<BR>Thanks for the help on this one Terry. Maybe I can get all this done before the end of the summer. Fingers crossed.<BR>Eric||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||05-22-2001||11:42 AM||||They sound like AC and TCC wires. I need to know if they are car wires or ECM wires.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Eric_PA||05-22-2001||05:32 PM||||I'm at home now and checked the ECM. It's an 8253.<P>The unknown wires are as follows:<BR>Brown/Black goes to car and ECM (they were both tied together on the connector)<BR>Violet -&gt;ECM Different wire from the next one, but same exact color)<BR>Violet -&gt;CAR<BR>3 light green -&gt;CAR<BR>Blue/Black -&gt;CAR<BR>Grey -&gt;CAR<BR>Black/Violet -&gt; CAR<BR>Blue -&gt; CAR<P>10 wires, i thought I was down to 8. My memory has failed me slightly.<BR>Eric<BR>||||reg||1
